WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.820 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  what's going on out there  it's been a few months since we last  jumped into the chaotic world of for  honor the closed alpha gave me many  enjoyable moments but it also left me  concerned about balancing issues in the  latest build we sat down with three new  characters a new multiplayer mode and  two single-player missions so without  further ado here's my take on how far  honor is shaping up if I had to pick one  thing that didn't work for me back when  I played the closed alpha three months  ago it would be character balancing  light armor characters such as the  Berserker could easily spam light  attacks and run circles around heavy  armored opponents such as the warden and  Raider to the point that during the last  few hours of that alpha no one wanted to  play as a heavy character if the other  team was made out of lights those  balancing issues for the most part have  been addressed in the latest build heavy  characters block more quickly and light  characters run through their stamina a  lot faster preventing them from doing  endless light swinging attacks on other  heroes medium characters such as the  Conqueror have also been given a damage  boost  however this character still has too big  of a tell with a long wind-up of where  he can swing his mace making it too easy  to read his moves there's still  balancing problems that need to be  addressed between light and heavy heroes  but for honor for the most part is  making progress  speaking of characters I got a chance to  play three new additions to the roster  the peacekeeper warlord and the shougo  key the peacekeeper is a fast assassin  hit-and-run kind of hero with a good  attack strength but low defense and  health she's excellent for harassing  enemies and capturing points in a flash  but can be brought down with just three  heavy attacks the warlord is a medium  attack and defensive hero he doesn't  excel in either strength or taking  damage over a long period of time like  other heroes but he does even out the  playing field with good crowd control  and the support role to other players in  need last but not least is Asha goki  one of the most powerful heavy hitters  with just three hits to practically any  character this hero can finish off any  foe he is the slowest moving and  swinging hero making it a tad too easy  to anticipate his moves but comboing him  with a light character Ally and you have  one of the most dangerous duos on the  field all three characters were fun to  play with each one filling a needed role  peacekeepers hit-and-run tactics warlord  playing support and they should go keep  playing the tank  if further balances out the growing  roster in a positive way despite the  fact that each character still needs a  little more fine-tuning  lost the new multiplayer mode I play was  called elimination elimination is a four  verse four with no capture points and no  npc minions pretty much team deathmatch  this mode was a blast allowing us to  take full customized heroes into battle  and brought some the best trash-talking  during my time playing it to  single-player missions were also on hand  raid the Raiders where you play surprise  the Raider class and sabotage where you  play as a peacekeeper the single-player  missions open up an interesting  narrative however as it stands they're  easily forgettable thanks in part to the  combat respawning and repetitive enemies  hurt this experience the most with a  dynasty warrior style set up waves of  dimwit enemies surround you only for  each one of them waiting for their  number to get called up like at the DMV  to get killed one out of every 20 foes  will fight you in a style similar to  what you could find online blocking  countering and unleashing special  attacks helps separate these foes from  the rest of the pack but with them far  and too few in between the drones of  mindless enemies it does nothing but  hurt the experience the narrative is  great so far but the gameplay needs some  heavy work to keep me interested from  start to finish  join us we are with you all in all I had  a great time with four honors  multiplayer the new character classes  new mode and balancing tweaks all played  a role in my enjoyment with the upcoming  release in February of 2017 there's  still a lot of time left for changes and  I'm looking forward to playing it again  are you looking forward to for honor  feel free to share your comments below  and for more on the game keep it here on  GameSpot  [Music]

